<title>UK: Rationalisation hits House of Fraser profits.</title>
<headline>Rationalisation hits House of Fraser profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to January 25, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.9 loss	   vs  5.0 profit</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.8		   vs  3.8</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 5.5		   vs  5.5</p>
<p> Pretax pre-exceps     14.8 profit	  vs 14.3 profit</p>
<p> Pretax post-exceps    38.4 loss	    vs 14.3 profit</p>
<p> Turnover		 781.4		   vs 748.9</p>
<p> Operating result	 24.2 profit	 vs 22.4 profit</p>
<p>NOTE - British department store group House of Fraser Plc said it charged 53.2 million stg in exceptional costs for rationalisation, including the costs of disposing of three stores, restructuring internal operations of all stores and 22 million stg for clearance of &quot;off-strategy&quot; stock.</p>
<p>The company said it made a pretax profit before exceptionals of 14.8 million stg, compared with 14 million stg last time and in line with market forecasts of 14 to 15 million stg and an unchanged dividend payout.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
